part.

"Modified Version" means any version of the Software that has been altered,
adapted, translated, or built upon, in source or compiled form.

"Substantial Portion" means any part of the Software that is independently
functional, readily recognizable as derived from the Software, or that
reproduces its distinctive structure, logic, or design in a way that a
reasonable developer would identify as taken from Pi-Dos. Small, generic code
fragments used purely to illustrate a general programming concept are not
considered a Substantial Portion.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software, or a Modified Version, that
is: (a) by or on behalf of a business or organization in the course of its
operations; (b) incorporated into a product or service that is sold, licensed,
or monetized in any way (including via advertising, subscriptions, or paid
support); or (c) otherwise intended to generate, or that does generate,
revenue or commercial advantage, whether directly or indirectly.

"You" means the individual or entity exercising any permission granted by
this license.

